+
+
+## Mathematical titles and list items
+
+`Title` and `BulletedList` now interpret their content as native `TexText`:
+prose can contain `$...$` or `$$...$$` mathematics, TeX text styling, and
+native commands. Previously these portal constructors used literal `Text`
+layout, so a fraction displayed backslashes and braces rather than a
+fraction. Their content now agrees with an independently constructed
+`TexText` at the same font size.
+
+Bullets and numbered labels remain bundled native text, and underlines
+remain native `Line` geometry. No `itemize` document, LaTeX invocation, or
+second layout engine is introduced. The existing arrangement, fade and
+underline configuration contracts remain intact. Mathematical titles
+publish per-primitive source spans through their part groups, excluding
+underlines, so source selection and recoloring can address an individual
+symbol rather than only a whole title part.
+
+Both constructors accept the same `template` and `additional_preamble`
+options as `TexText`. A list's preamble is shared by configuration, not by
+mutable expansion state: an inline definition in one item never leaks to
+another. Invalid native mathematics produces a precise construction error,
+not literal text or blank output. Literal backslashes and dollar signs
+must be escaped using the native TexText grammar; use `Text` when the
+content is intended to display source code verbatim.
+
+Rust callers can explicitly use `Title::build_tex` and
+`BulletedList::build_tex`. Their existing `build(&FontBook)` APIs retain
+literal-text semantics for callers deliberately composing plain text.
